id: ops-ilcm
title: Windows consumers gate flakes when a packed npm install exceeds its 180 s spawn timeout
description: "test/duplication-packed.acceptance.ts runs npm install --ignore-scripts for a synthetic packed consumer with a 180 s spawn timeout. On a Windows runner the install exceeded the timeout, so spawnSync returned status null and the exact-status assertion failed, turning the windows-consumers job red for machine load rather than for code. A failed-job rerun on the identical head passed in 2m55. Same class as the busy-machine timing flake already tracked, but a distinct timeout site; consider retrying installs or raising the timeout on windows runners."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: ci,flake,test,windows
created_at: "2026-10-19T23:24:20.440Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T19:22:21.841Z"
author: pi-agent
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-22T19:15:57.077Z",codex-agent,"Additional occurrence while validating PR 192 at unchanged head 87c8dac: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/39837214110 . Windows consumers Node 22 failed in test/duplication-packed.acceptance.ts at npm install --ignore-scripts with status null versus expected 0; the launcher retains its 180-second timeout. Node 26 Windows consumers and all four npm/Bun release gates passed. Failed-job-only rerun requested without code changes. Reusing this existing issue rather than creating a duplicate; no timeout or assertion relaxation is included in the evidence-expiry review fix."
  "2026-10-22T19:22:21.830Z",codex-agent,"The failed-job-only retry of Windows 22 passed at the identical 87c8dac head: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/39837214110 . The full four-job matrix is green, including both npm/Bun release gates on Node 22 and 26. No code, timeout or assertion changes were needed. This confirms an intermittent packed-install failure signature; the broader timeout robustness issue remains open."
body: ""
